      "description": "Personal Information Protection and Electronic Documents Act",
      "weight": 100,
      "data": {
        "official_name": "Personal Information Protection and Electronic Documents Act",
        "common_name": "PIPEDA",
        "alternate_names": [
          "S.C. 2000, c. 5"
        ],
        "description": "Canada's baseline federal private-sector data-protection law, in force since 2001. Governs collection, use, and disclosure of personal information in the course of commercial activity.",
        "notes": "The federal government has made multiple attempts to replace PIPEDA (CPPA under Bill C-27, died on the order paper Jan 2025; now Bill C-36 / PPCDA as of June 2026) — see secid:regulation/priv.gc.ca/ppcda-bill-c36. PIPEDA remains in force until a successor passes.",
        "urls": [
          {
            "type": "legal_text",
            "url": "https://laws-lois.justice.gc.ca/eng/acts/p-8.6/"
          }
        ],
        "examples": []
      },
